    "# Library Management System\n",
    "**Console-based Python project | OOP + Python fundamentals**\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements a library system with books, members, borrowing and returning, searching, input validation, and optional JSON persistence.\n",
    "\n",
    "**OOP concepts included**\n",
    "- Encapsulation: internal state uses `_is_available` and `_borrowed_books`.\n",
    "- Inheritance: `PremiumMember` inherits from `Member`.\n",
    "- Polymorphism: `PremiumMember` overrides `get_borrow_limit()`.\n",
    "- `__str__`: readable object representations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells from top to bottom. The final cell starts the interactive menu."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "94ecb8dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "240a615a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_FILE = Path(\"library_data.json\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "10956126",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Book class"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1e2f70ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Book:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, book_id, title, author, is_available=True):\n",
    "        self.book_id = str(book_id)\n",
    "        self.title = title\n",
    "        self.author = author\n",
    "        self._is_available = bool(is_available)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def borrow(self):\n",
    "        if not self._is_available:\n",
    "            return False\n",
    "        self._is_available = False\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "\n",
    "    def return_book(self):\n",
    "        if self._is_available:\n",
    "            return False\n",
    "        self._is_available = True\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "\n",
    "    def is_available(self):\n",
    "        return self._is_available\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __str__(self):\n",
    "        status = \"Available\" if self._is_available else \"Borrowed\"\n",
    "        return f\"[{self.book_id}] {self.title} — {self.author} | Status: {status}\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5537787c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Member classes (inheritance and polymorphism)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bb3fc3ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Member:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, member_id, name):\n",
    "        self.member_id = str(member_id)\n",
    "        self.name = name\n",
    "        self._borrowed_books = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    def get_borrow_limit(self):\n",
    "        return 3\n",
    "\n",
    "    def borrow_book(self, book):\n",
    "        if len(self._borrowed_books) >= self.get_borrow_limit():\n",
    "            return False, f\"Borrowing limit reached ({self.get_borrow_limit()} books).\"\n",
    "        if not book.borrow():\n",
    "            return False, \"This book is already borrowed.\"\n",
    "        self._borrowed_books.append(book)\n",
    "        return True, f'\"{book.title}\" borrowed successfully.'\n",
    "\n",
    "    def return_book(self, book):\n",
    "        if book not in self._borrowed_books:\n",
    "            return False, \"This member has not borrowed that book.\"\n",
    "        if not book.return_book():\n",
    "            return False, \"The book is already marked as available.\"\n",
    "        self._borrowed_books.remove(book)\n",
    "        return True, f'\"{book.title}\" returned successfully.'\n",
    "\n",
    "    def list_borrowed_books(self):\n",
    "        return list(self._borrowed_books)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __str__(self):\n",
    "        return (f\"Member ID: {self.member_id} | Name: {self.name} | \"\n",
    "                f\"Borrowed: {len(self._borrowed_books)}/{self.get_borrow_limit()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class PremiumMember(Member):\n",
    "    # Overrides the parent method: this is polymorphism.\n",
    "    def get_borrow_limit(self):\n",
    "        return 5\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __str__(self):\n",
    "        return (f\"Premium {super().__str__()}\")"
   ]
  },
